                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.description.abstract" : [ {
                  "value" : "Summary of the Indian Contract Act, 1872. \n\nBasic Information\n•\tAct Name: The Indian Contract Act\n•\tAct No. & Year: Act No. 9 of 1872\n•\tEnactment Date: 25th April, 1872\n•\tCommencement Date: 1st day of September, 1872\n•\tExtent: Whole of India (with historical exceptions, now omitted as of Act 34 of 2019)\n2.\tInterpretation Clause (Partial):\n•\tProposal: Defined as one person signifying to another their willingness to do or abstain from doing something to obtain assent.\n3.\tSaving Clause: - Nothing in the Act affects provisions of any Statute, Act, or Regulation not expressly repealed, nor any usage or custom of trade, nor any incident of a contract not inconsistent with the Act.\n4.\tRelation to Other Acts: - The Transfer of Property Act, 1882: Certain chapters/sections related to contracts are considered part of this Act where the former is in force.\n•\tExtensions and Amendments: Mentioned for various regions (e.g., Berar, Dadra and Nagar Haveli, Goa, Daman and Diu, etc.), indicating the Act's applicability and updates over time.",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.identifier.act_id" : [ {
                  "value" : "AC_CEN_3_20_00035_187209_1523268996428",
                  "language" : null,
                  "authority" : null,
                  "confidence" : -1,
                  "place" : 0
                } ],
                "dc.identifier.act_number" : [ {
